{
 "spec": "services",
 "file": "logging",
 "notes": "L-6 and L-5 (RT2, RU3): a log line is a map of named fields; L-6's table is the complete set of field names each service may write, with domains, and a line with any other field or a value outside its domain is forbidden. One allowed and one forbidden line per service row, plus the aggregator and gateway cases of L-5: never a count of accepted ballots for a deck or a round, exact or bucketed, before or after the final version; for ballot intake no line per request, no per-request minute and no count per deck, round or path; rejections counted by code per deck only for malformed, too_large, rejected and forbidden; closed and conflict counted at no grain, appearing only in the service's daily total (rejected_count with no deck and no code). The gateway logs a path and result code with no connection identifier, or counts per path, nothing for a ballot-intake path and no intake counter at any grain: ballot requests appear only inside its daily total of all requests (count with no path). `rule` is L-5 where that rule names the failure (every L-5 failure is also an L-6 failure) and L-6 otherwise. Readings the spec leaves open: the delivery row defers to chat.md \u00a712.9's error-log row, which names no fields (the reference uses service, day, code, minute, context); `day` is a day number or YYYY-MM-DD; `code` is an error code string or an HTTP status; `minute` is a Unix time that is a multiple of 60; the resolver's after-24-hours shape is exactly {cid, count}.",
